      explanation: `<div style="border-radius:10px; box-shadow:0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; overflow:hidden"><div style="background-color:#01506e; border-radius:8px 8px 0 0; color:white; padding:20px"><h1 style="color:white; margin:0">Cash and Cash Equivalents: What to Include?</h1></div><div style="background-color:white; padding:20px"><div style="background-color:#f9f9f9; border-left:5px solid #0099d4; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Correct Answer</h3><p style="margin:0"><span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">✓</span> <span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">$8,120</span></p></div><div style="background-color:#f0f7fa; border-left:5px solid #68d3a7; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><p style="margin:0">Overview: Cash and cash equivalents are assets that are immediately available to pay bills or run daily operations. Think: cash in the bank, petty cash, and certain highly liquid investments.</p></div><div style="background-color:#f9f9f9; border-left:5px solid #0099d4; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Step-by-Step Analysis</h3><p style="margin:0">Start with the total of all possible cash-like items: Cash in bank: $3,000 (Yes, fully available), Petty cash: $120 (Yes, on hand and available), Money market account: $10,000 (Partially, see below), Postdated checks: $500 (No, not usable until check date).</p><p style="margin:0">Identify restrictions: $5,000 of the money market account is set aside (restricted) as a compensating balance for a loan due in three years. This means it&#x27;s not available for immediate use.</p><div style="background-color:white; border:1px solid #dddddd; border-radius:5px; font-family:monospace; margin:0 0 12px 0; padding:12px; text-align:center"><strong>Calculate cash and cash equivalents: Cash in bank + Petty cash + (Money market account - Restricted portion) = $3,000 + $120 + ($10,000 - $5,000) = $8,120.</strong></div></div><div style="background-color:#f5f9fc; border-left:5px solid #207bb5; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Calculation Summary</h3><table cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse; margin-top:15px; width:100%"><thead><tr><th style="border-bottom:2px solid #01506e; padding:10px; text-align:left">Item</th><th style="border-bottom:2px solid #01506e; padding:10px; text-align:left">Amount</th><th style="border-bottom:2px solid #01506e; padding:10px; text-align:left">Included?</th><th style="border-bottom:2px solid #01506e; padding:10px; text-align:left">Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Cash in bank</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">$3,000</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px"><span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">✓</span> Yes</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Fully available</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Petty cash</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">$120</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px"><span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">✓</span> Yes</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">On hand and available</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Money market account (unrestricted)</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">$5,000</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px"><span style="color:#4caf50; font-weight:bold">✓</span> Yes</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Liquid portion available for use</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Money market account (restricted)</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">$5,000</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px"><span style="color:#f44336; font-weight:bold">✗</span> No</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Compensating balance for loan</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Postdated checks</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">$500</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px"><span style="color:#f44336; font-weight:bold">✗</span> No</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Not yet available for use</td></tr><tr><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">Total Cash &amp; Cash Equivalents</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px">$8,120</td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px"></td><td style="border-bottom:1px solid #dddddd; padding:10px"></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="background-color:#eef9f2; border-left:5px solid #68d3a7; border-radius:8px; margin-bottom:20px; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:#01506e; margin:0 0 12px 0">Common Mistakes</h3><p style="margin:0">Mistake: Including postdated checks. Why wrong: Postdated checks aren&#x27;t available until their date arrives: think of them as &#x27;future money.&#x27;</p><p style="margin:0">Mistake: Including both postdated checks and restricted cash. Why wrong: Neither are available now.</p><p style="margin:0">Mistake: Adding up everything, ignoring restrictions and timing. Why wrong: Overstates available cash by including restricted and unavailable funds.</p></div><div style="background-color:#01506e; border-radius:0 0 8px 8px; color:white; padding:15px"><h3 style="color:white; margin:0 0 12px 0">Summary</h3><p style="margin:0">Only include cash and investments that are available for immediate use.</p><p style="margin:0">Exclude: Restricted funds (e.g., compensating balances for long-term loans), Postdated checks (not cash yet).</p><p style="margin:0">Remember: If you can&#x27;t spend it right now, it&#x27;s NOT a cash equivalent.</p></div></div></div>`,
